  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Calculation (Strategy Solitaire). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Calculation (also known as Strategy or 'Broken Intervals') is a unique solitaire card game that deviates from standard 'Klondike' mechanics. Unlike most solitaires that build in simple 1-2-3 steps, each of the four foundation piles in Calculation builds at a different mathematical interval: Pile 1 goes 1, 2, 3...; Pile 2 goes 2, 4, 6...; Pile 3 goes 3, 6, 9...; and Pile 4 goes 4, 8, Q... It is a game of pure skill and memory where the layout of the 'Waste' piles determines victory.",
    objective: 'Move all 52 cards onto the four foundation piles by building each foundation in its fixed interval sequence (Ace+1, 2+2, 3+3, 4+4) until every card is played; the game is lost if no further play is possible.',
    gameplay: '1. Turn up a card from the Stock.\n2. If it can be played on a Foundation, do so.\n3. If not, you MUST place it on one of the 4 Waste piles.\n4. You can only move the TOP card of a Waste pile to a Foundation. You cannot move cards between Waste piles.',
    keyRules: [
      'Four foundations build by intervals: +1, +2, +3, +4. Only top of waste movable to foundation.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
